The MIT license above covers ONLY the original work in this repository: the
protocol documentation, the Python auth-shim / world-server stack, the
reverse-engineering and analysis tooling, and the schema/structure exports we
authored.

This project is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to Project
Ascension or Blizzard Entertainment. World of Warcraft, Project Ascension, and
their related assets are the property of their respective owners. No game
client, MPQ/DBC game data, models, textures, audio, UI art, or other
copyrighted Blizzard or Ascension material is distributed with this software.
To run this stack you must supply those files from your own legally obtained
client; see data/MANIFEST.md.

This is a preservation and interoperability project, created after Project
Ascension's shutdown on 2026-09-04, for making a client you own talk to a
server you run. The small data exports under data/ and server/data/ are derived
from the client's own files and can be regenerated from your own client with
the tools in tools/ (see data/MANIFEST.md).
